        // Since we cannot control block.timestamp dynamically in a single call, we use the current
        // block.timestamp via block.timestamp opcode, but the precondition for success is that
        // block.timestamp > beforePastBlockTime. In the test, beforePastBlockTime is the value stored
        // at deployment (initialized to 0 for fresh contract? Actually constructor doesn't set it, so it's 0).
        // So block.timestamp > 0 always. Thus for a fresh contract, the condition block.timestamp > pastBlockTime
